Hello there Warlords!

We will update the game during our maintenance on October 29th, which will last for 2 hours and run between 12:00-14:00 (UTC+8). After the maintenance we will give all players 5,000 Bronze Coins and 200 Honour as compensation for any inconvenience caused. Be sure arrange your time accordingly. The update will contain the following: 

1) Ranked Battle Rank Rewards

Following this week's maintenance you will be able to claim your Ranked Battle rank rewards. To view and claim your rewards, simply navigate the following menus [Battle] -> [Ranked Battle] -> [Rank Rewards]. Ranks and their rewards are as follows: 
- Sergeant Rewards: Honour x500, Bronze Coin x25,000;
- Vanguard Rank Rewards: Random Rare Artillery Chest x2, Bronze Coin x30,000;
- Captain Rank Reward: Random Epic Artillery Chest x1, Bronze Coin x50,000;
- Warlord Rank Reward: Random Epic Artillery Chest x2, Honour x1,000;
- Cadet-General Rank Reward: Unit Medal x60, Treatise x1;
- General Rank Reward: Powdered Silver x50, Treatise x2;
- Captain-General Rank Reward: Doctrine Water x5, Treatise x3;
- Lord Commander Rank Reward: Limited-time title [Legacy of Fire - Platinum Vanguard], Treatise x5;
- Marshal Rank Reward: Limited-time title [Legacy of Fire - Platinum Hero], Epic Hero Schematic Crate x1.

2) Territory War Ruling House Improvements

When a Liege or Seneschal of a ruling house declares war, they may adjust the settings of that assault:
- Only alliance members can join.
- Only alliance members and their friends can join.
- Anyone not at war with their alliance can join.
- Anyone can join.

※Having declared, the Liege or Seneschal may adjust this setting at any time under My House - Battles.

3) New Character Creation Improvements

In order to make it easier for newer players to take part in heated battles, newly created characters will be able to choose an extra Chivalric Era unit from the following: Ironcap Spearmen, Squires, and Halberdiers. The unit they select will serve as their initial unit in Expedition.

What's more, characters created after September 29 that have selected a region will receive the following compensation reward: [Expedition Unit Selection Box]. When opened the player may choose between one of the following rewards: Ironcap Spearmen, Squires, Halberdiers, or Unit Medals.

4) Beginner Quests & Hero Improvements

Beginner Hero Improvements:
So as to improve the beginner experience for many of the heroes, we have decided to adjust rank I and II of the following skills:

Dual Blades:
1. Bo-Shurikens I: 189% Base Damage + 1,142 Piercing Damage, 8 sec CD → 169% Base Damage + 1,490 Piercing Damage, 7 sec CD;
2. Bo-Shurikens II: 189% Base Damage + +1,364 Piercing Damage, 7 sec CD → 179% Base Damage + +1,542 Piercing Damage, 6 sec CD;
3. Skylark I: 9 sec CD → 8 sec CD;
4. Skylark II: 8 sec CD → 7 sec CD;
5. Replaced the basic skill Butterfly with Great Thunderbolt.

Longsword & Shield:
1. With Valour I:
One-hit attack, 100% Basic + 954 Slashing Damage, 28 sec CD → Two-hit Combo with each hit dealing 83% Basic + 1,086 Slashing Damage, 20 sec CD;
2. With Valour II:
Two-hit Combo with each hit dealing 100% Basic + 1,107 Slashing Damage, 24 sec CD → Two-hit Combo with each hit dealing 93% Basic + 1,294 Slashing Damage, 20 sec CD;
3. Paladin I:
One-hit attack, 75% Basic +758 Slashing Damage -> Two-hit Combo, with the first attack dealing 60% Basic + 858 Slashing Damage, and the second hit dealing 90% Basic + 1,124 Slashing Damage;
4. Paladin II:
First hit dealing 75% Basic + 903 Slashing Damage, second hit dealing 105% Basic + 1,264 Slashing Damage -> First hit dealing 75% Basic + 953 Slashing Damage, second hit dealing 105% Basic + 1,364 Slashing Damage 
5. Martial Prowess I:
60% Basic + 607 Slashing Damage, 1% Recovery -> 50% Basic + 817 Slashing Damage, 3% Recovery;
6. Martial Prowess II:
60% Basic + +722 Slashing Damage, 2% Recovery -> 55% Basic + +825 Slashing Damage, 3% Recovery;

Poleaxe:
1. Bec de Corbin I:
One-hit attack, 113% Basic + 1,515 Slashing Damage, 28 sec CD → Three-hit Combo with each hit dealing 73% Basic + 1,212 Slashing Damage, 24 sec CD;
2. Bec de Corbin II:
Two-hit Combo with each hit dealing 113% Base + 1,699 Slashing Damage, 28 sec CD → Three-hit Combo with each hit dealing 93% Basic + 1,499 Slashing Damage, 24 sec CD;
3. Weapon Dance I:
24 sec CD → 20 sec CD;
4. Weapon Dance II
20 sec CD → 18 sec CD;

5) Using Blank Signaculum

Currently, you may exchange [Blank Signaculum] for [Unit Medals] from within the Excavate -> Redeem menu.
40 [Blank Signaculum] can be exchanged for one [Unit Medal], and this can be done a total of 60 times each week.

6) Unit/Hero Bug Fixes & Improvements

1. Resolved an issue where the Elite Kriegsrat Fusiliers' character model would disappear from Unit Details;
2. Resolved an issue where damage increase of the Barcyan Narfan Guard: Ablaze doctrine didn't reflect that of the description;
3. Resolved an issue where, after having trained the Everflame and Immortal nodes of Barcyan Narfan Guard, their ability graph would point toward Defence. This has been corrected and the ability graph should now point toward Attack;
4. Improved the description for Barcyan Narfan Guard training nodes (percentage increases are based on the unit's base damage so the actual numbers haven't been changed):
- Burn. Previously, the description said 'Each level increases burn damage by 5%', this has now been changed to 'Each level increases burn damage by 80'; 
- Ablaze. Previously, the description said 'Increases burn damage by 30%', this has now been changed to 'Increases burn damage by 480'.
5、Resolved an issue where the Spear Sergeants and Men-at-Arms units could be promoted, and in doing so they would become unsealed;
6、Resolved an issue where the Dragon's Leap's extra effect for nodachi heroes didn't work as intended (If under the effect of [Bloodcraze], [Bloodcraze] is consumed, granting immunity toward all crowd control effects for the skill's duration).

7) General Bug Fixes

1. Resolved an issue where fief icons would disappear from the World Map when pressing on fief info in the chat;
2. Resolved an issue where resource site yields didn't refresh as intended;
3. Resolved an issue where some artilleries were missing from the crafting menu of the following fiefs:
- Méhkerék: Optimal Mortar;
- Gyoma: Optimal Mortar;
- Kiralyfalva: Optimal Mortar;
- Hévíz: Optimal Mortar;
- Gaoda: Optimal Cannon;
- Louge: Optimal Cannon;
4. Resolved an issue where the statistics of some achievements were displayed incorrectly;
5. Resolved an issue where there were no sound of footsteps when blocking with some weapons;
6. Resolved an issue where the sounds of artilleries in Siege Battle could be heard from too far away. The sound effects of setting up and kicking down ladders, and flaming pitch on city walls have also been improved;
7. Resolved an issue where the crafting tax of Continopolis displayed as 0% when it was actually 100%;
8. Resolved an issue when the same Watchman would appear after teleporting from the Border Posts Segnia and Imre Kastély.
9. Resolved an issue where units would charge in the opposite direction when the hero is standing with its back toward a wall while issuing the Charge skill;
10. Resolved an issue where defenders' units couldn't interact with some of their supply points during battles with multiple fronts.

8) Stage Bug Fixes & Improvements

1. Resolved an issue where, when switching to the World Map while on a voyage, sailing animation and sounds would be re-played;
2. Resolved an issue with the Hévíz map in Territory War. Its displayed occupation time differed from the actual time it would take to occupy it, but both should now be 60 seconds;
3. Resolved an issue with the defender's default resurrection point during the first phase of the Siege of Augolia stage. The resurrection point has now been moved to inside the city.

9) General Improvements

1. The ranking of the top players in Ranked Battle should now be displayed in a clearer fashion;
2. Added further information regarding Territory War, Military Exercise, and Eclipse Exercise to the Battle menu. Check it out if you're unfamiliar with how these modes work;
3. Improved the names and descriptions of some attires in the Store;
4. Added a Quick Buy feature for when you have run out of Return Orders and Camp Migration Tokens;
5. For Barcyan Narfan Guard challenges and quests, completion conditions have been changed from 'take any of the seasonal Barcyan units' to 'take any of the Barcyan or Maltese units'.

10) Siege Battle Map Pool Changes

[Continopolis (Siege)] will be added to the current map pool.

Hello there Warlords!
    We will update the game during our maintenance on October 22nd, which will last for 2 hours and run between 12:00-14:00 (UTC+8). After the maintenance we will give all players 5,000 Bronze Coins and 200 Honour as compensation for any inconvenience caused. Be sure arrange your time accordingly. The update will contain the following: 

1) Halloween Event

1. The Halloween event stage Attack of the Crows will be available for a limited time.
The villagers planned a great holiday feast for the glory of the saints. However, the Mercenary Guild's spies sent a messing, warning them that a group of bandits saw this as their chance to plunder and pillage.
Heroes of justice and glory will not stand idly by as the clutches of evil work. Warlords, band together and protect the village!
※Run time: 12:00-20:00 every day from October 26th to November 2nd. You only gain rewards from the first three times you enter it each day. Jack-o-Lanterns will also drop when playing the event stage. Plus tons of Halloween gifts!

2. Limited-time Sale on Halloween Attire
Between October 26th and November 12th, the Auctioneers will unseal their Halloween treasury once more. Having been sealed for one year, the limited Halloween attires once again hit the shelves:
Hero Attire: Plague Doctor; Unit Attire: Revenant; Hero Horse Attire: Plague!

