{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/35323464/50ef5cce7b725ce70625f30ee4ec6f937eb952a5.jpg

2) Update to Matchmaking Map Rotation

- New maps this rotation: Wall Fort (Siege), Border Fort (Siege), Steinburg Village (Field), Valley Fortress (Ranked);
-- Maps removed this rotation: White Elk Fort (Siege), Allenburg (Siege).

3) General Improvements

1.  Territory War Ruling House Improvements
- We have removed the restriction where the ruling house could not kick "Players with a contribution of 20%, and at least 10 players of their house are present on the battlefield";
- Previously the ruling house could not kick members of a "house that has a contribution of 50%," but this has now been changed to 80%;
2.  Improved the textual display of artillery rarity: these should now be shown as uncommon, rare, epic, and legendary;
3.  Adjusted the location of Arany Pajzsok and surrounding resources sites (in Ungverija);
4.  Altered the difficulty of some quests of Hero's Path:
- Collect 5 resources of rare quality has now been changed to uncommon quality;
- Become the MVP 4 times in Siege or Field Battles has been changed to 2 times;
- Increased the Bronze Coin reward from Hero's Path quests;
- Hero's Path quest: Add 3 friends has been changed to 'Add 1 friend;
- Hero's Path quest: Previously, kits and artilleries had to be crafted to count toward progress. Now, obtaining one of the right quality also counts toward progress;
5.  Decreased the music document size when pre-loading the client;
6.  With the opening of Bartholia, many new trade routes are available in Conqueror's Blade. The cities of Liangyun, Ungverija, and The Borderlands worked day and night to create their trade posts. You can now head to these to procure additional resources;
7. During the third stage of the Spear Sergeants promotion challenge, 
"In Siege Battle or Field Battles, take the Spear Sergeants unit into battle 7 times while getting a KD of more than 1," has been changed to: "In Siege Battle or Field Battles, take the Spear Sergeants unit into battle and win 4 times";
8.  Removed the item weight from hero weapons and equipment;
9.  When the attributes gained from a seasonal doctrine exceed that of a permanent doctrine, attributes gained now reflect that of the seasonal doctrine;
10.  Named the mountains, rivers, lakes, and seas of Bartholia.

4) Hero Bug Fixes & Balance Changes

1.  Resolved an issue where, when a hero changed from Burning to Ablaze, no animation of them being terrified would be played;
2.  Nodachi Hero Balance Changes:
- Added a new effect to Monstrous Blade I and II: Consuming [Bloodcraze] will now heal the user;
- Added a new effect to Dragon's Leap: Using the skill while under the effect of [Bloodcraze] will consume [Bloodcraze] and grant immunity to all crowd control effects for the skill's duration;
- Added a new effect to Avalanche: Hits against enemies grants a stack of [Health Drain];
3. - Resolved an issue where no sound effect would be played when blocking with Dual Blades or Mauls.

5) Unit Bug Fixes

- Resolved an issue with the voice effect played when units are affected by Ablaze;
- Resolved an issue where flames left behind by Barcyan Wildflame were not affected by rainy weather;
- Resolved an issue where, when Spear Sergeants attacked an enemy while in a tight formation, some units would remain stuck in place and stop moving if the Cover Commander skill was used;
- Resolved an issue where the following units could not properly interact with supply points: Spahks Cavalry, Winged Hussars, Selemchid Cavalry, Falconettii Gunners, and Fortebraccio Pikemen;
- Resolved an issue where, when a Burning Barcyan Wildflame was set Ablaze, their oil canister wouldn't explode upon death.

6) Stage Bug Fixes

- Resolved an issue where the location to interact with large artilleries were wrong on Fort stages in Bartholia;
- Resolved an issue where some pre-set artilleries in Field Battle (matchmaking) would affect unit move speed;
- Resolved an issue where Fishing Ports also had fief tribute;
- Resolved an issue where players with all units could not go into battle with Auxiliary Units, and this has now been changed to: "take Auxiliary units or Chivalric Era or later units into battle 1 time";
- Resolved an issue where fief quests in Bartholia did not reward kit boxes. The correct rewards will be available first thing on Monday;
- Resolved an issue where the Watchman would disappear when going to Bartholia from the Segnia border post in The Borderlands;
- Resolved an issue where the crafting ability of Hévíz, Louge, and Gaoda as seen on the World Map was different from their actual values;
- Resolved an issue where, when purchasing items at a trade post with a fully loaded wagon, resource piles couldn't be withdrawn;
- Resolved an issue where players on sea voyages could be pursued by others;
- Resolved an issue where the yellow text of compared equipment would disappear when adding equipment to the salvage list;
- Resolved an issue where the "Go" command would not appear while clicking a fief in Bartholia while the character was not in Bartholia;
- Resolved an issue where the Imperial Restorationists icon had disappeared from War Info of fiefs in Territory War;
- Resolved an issue where only the leader of Imperial Restorationists could declare war;
- Resolved an issue where trade posts and harbors around Continopolis weren't displayed as intended;
- Resolved an issue where resources sites in Territory War could only be force collected yet could not be collected normally;
- Resolved an issue where the ladders of Continopolis underground weren't displayed as intended;
- Resolved an issue where, when a harness was under repair, the mount using it would not be displayed properly;
- Resolved an issue where the Hero's Path - Path of Justice quest 'Join a House/Cohort' would only be completed if joining one while being online.

Greetings Warlords!
    We will update the game during our maintenance on September 24th, which will last for 4 hours and run between 12:00-16:00 (UTC+8). After the maintenance we will give all players 10,000 Bronze Coins and 400 Honour as compensation for any inconvenience caused. Be sure arrange your time accordingly. The update will contain the following: 

1) Server Transfers

After the maintenance on September 24th, we will be transferring characters that signed up for character transfers between September 17th and September 23rd to their target servers. Restated Server Transfer Info:
1. During server transfer, only items and resources in your Inventory, Supply Dump, and Wagon will be brought. Items and resources already listed with the Auctioneers cannot be brought, neither can resources in Resource Piles. Mail and their attachments will be transferred to the new server.
2. Upon successful server transfer, the character's friend and blacklists will be cleared. Your character will be removed from your House, Alliance/Imperial Restorationists. Upon logging in to the new server, you will once again have to choose a region.
3. Should a character with the same name as yours exist on the server you transfer to, a string of digits will be added to your name. On the day of the server transfer we will then issue you a New Identity Document x1.
4. Once the server transfer has been completed, the ID of all characters on all servers will be generated anew.

2) Attire Product Cycle Info

Auctioneers Appearance Product Cycle: The following appearance-altering products will be available from 09/24/2020 - 10/22/2020 at discounted prices: 
- The Armour appearance [Runic Knight] for 1,580 Sovereigns (20% Off);
- The Unit appearance [Fleur-de-Lys Attire] for 1,020 Sovereigns (20% Off);
- The Longbow appearance [Sanguine Scorpion] for 280 Sovereigns (20% Off);
- The Short Bow appearance [Amethystine Shortbow] for 280 Sovereigns (20% Off);
-The mount appearance [Chivalric Set] for 1340 Sovereigns (20% Off);

- The following items will be taken off the shelves: The Armour appearance [Varangian Attire], the Weapon attires [Blue Steel] and [Golden Phoenix], the banner attire [Holy Mountain], and the mount appearance [Draconic Set].

3) General Improvements

- The Finals of Conqueror's Blade's S3 House Invitation Tournament will be played on the eve of September 26th, which means that Conquest will be unavailable on that day;
- Conqueror's Journey Battlefield within the [Excavation] menu will be closing after this maintenance;
- The Artisan's Black Feather Dance attire, and the Thousand Spire Attire Treasure exchange concludes on September 29th.

    New season is just around the horizon, please stay tuned!

Hello there Warlords!
    We will update the game during our maintenance on September 10th, which will last for 2 hours and run between 12:00-14:00 (UTC+8). After the maintenance we will give all players 5,000 Bronze Coins and 200 Honour as compensation for any inconvenience caused. Be sure arrange your time accordingly. The update will contain the following: 

1) Campaigns Season Results

The season will be concluding at the time of the September 17th maintenance.
You will not be able to gain Glory from Battles, Alliance Quests, Free Battles, Conquest or by leveling up starting from September 17th until the next season begins.
Glory can still be earned via Weekly Challenges, Battle Disciplines, and Janissaries Rules.
The Seasonal Store will also be available until the new season begins.

Imperial Dawn for this season's Campaign will begin on September 14th, 00:00, the reward will be issued after maintenance on September 17th. One thing differs from previous seasons: at the time of this season's conclusion, we will be issuing Empire Coins to players in accordance to the number, type, and level of fiefs their Alliance/Cohort occupy.
The number of fiefs an Alliance/Cohort possess will be counted as it stands on September 14th, 23:59.
Imperial Restorationists will gain rewards for all liberated fiefs within their Cohort that are not located within a safe zone.
Fief level 1-5 cities: Empire Coin x30;
Fief level 6-15 cities: Empire Coin x50;
Fief level 1-5 forts: Empire Coin x30;
Fief level 6-15 forts: Empire Coin x50;
Fief level 1-5 villages: Empire Coin x15;
Fief level 6-15 villages: Empire Coin x30;
Empire Coins can be redeemed for various resources within the "Conquer Cities to Get Rewards" event. Including Treatises, Powdered Silver, Rare Equipment Schematics, Hero XP Cards, and Unit XP Cards.
Rewards can be redeemed from September 17th (after maintenance) until the next season begins.

Title/Rank Rewards: 
Free Houses Rewards:
A crown will be issued in according to your title, and can be used until the end of the next season.
The Hegemon and Chamberlain titles have special unlock conditions:
Hegemon: Must be the liege of a ruling house. The alliance must have an Influence of ≥25,000 and have captured the Conqueror's City;
Once a liege have been granted the title of Hegemon, seneschals in that alliance will be granted the title of General;
Chamberlain: Must be the liege of a ruling house. The alliance must have an Influence greater than 20,000 or have captured the Conqueror's City while not qualifying for the Hegemon title.

Imperial Restorationists Rewards:
A crown will be issued in according to your rank, and can be used until the end of the next season. (Players with a rank of Stalwart/Junior Captain or lower may not receive this reward) 


Seasonal Title Reward:
Free Houses Title: All members of the alliance that in the end occupies Conqueror's City will gain the Blood of the Empire Destiny title.

Imperial Restorationists Title:
Those of the Imperial Restorationists who take part in the battle for Conqueror's City will gain the permanent title of Blood of the Empire Volunteer. Should you be among the Imperial Restorationists who in the end protect Shield of the Capital, you will gain the permanent title of Blood of the Empire Royal Guard. Should you in the end manage to protect Conqueror's City, you will receive the permanent title of Blood of the Empire Legion.

While Imperial Dawn is running, Military Exercises and Conquest will still be available until the next season begins.
Military Exercise will be available at September 15th.
Conquest will run as normal on every Tuesday and Saturday after September 15th.
Neither Conqueror's City nor Shield of the Capital will be available in Conquest during this time.
